- Ask for an internship?

00:01:45.511 --> 00:01:48.108
- You ask for work?
Don't you just ask for work?

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.533
- [India] I guess because a lot people

00:01:49.533 --> 00:01:50.432
come to companies and it says like

00:01:50.432 --> 00:01:51.649
you need this many years of experience.

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:52.843
- Oh, I see.
- [Gary] I see.

00:01:52.843 --> 00:01:53.960
- [India] But how do
you get that experience

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:54.761
if nobody wants to hire
you because everybody--

00:01:54.761 --> 00:01:56.324
- When you're 18.

00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:57.380
- [India] Yeah.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.926
- I got an answer to this, I mean

00:01:58.926 --> 00:02:01.045
I think that we now live in a world--

00:02:01.045 --> 00:02:02.498
Casey, how many people,

00:02:02.498 --> 00:02:05.678
how many people hit you
up on Twitter, email,

00:02:05.678 --> 00:02:08.673
other platforms, comments and YouTube,

00:02:08.673 --> 00:02:10.205
you must have a gadrillion.

00:02:10.205 --> 00:02:12.179
How many times have you in your career--

00:02:12.179 --> 00:02:14.246
When would you say that
you started really building

00:02:14.246 --> 00:02:16.892
into a place where people
were really pinging you?

00:02:16.892 --> 00:02:19.214
Is this now a two, three,
four year phenomenon for you?

00:02:19.214 --> 00:02:20.004
- For work?

00:02:20.004 --> 00:02:20.933
- Yes.

00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:23.533
Not for work, more like
people that are fans of you,

00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:24.903
clearly at this point.

00:02:24.903 --> 00:02:27.086
- It's been a long time.

00:02:27.086 --> 00:02:28.688
- How long, do you think?

00:02:28.688 --> 00:02:30.846
- I mean, I think since the
first video I made went viral

00:02:30.846 --> 00:02:31.980
over 10 years ago.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.447
- Got it. So, it's been pretty
consistent since then?

00:02:33.447 --> 00:02:34.283
- Yeah.
- Good,

00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:36.606
how many times have you
randomly done stuff?

00:02:36.606 --> 00:02:38.289
Yes, met someone, got on a phone.

00:02:38.289 --> 00:02:39.485
How many times?

00:02:39.485 --> 00:02:41.156
- Now, if I could count that, Gary.

00:02:41.156 --> 00:02:43.269
More than I could ever keep track of.

00:02:43.269 --> 00:02:44.755
- That's your answer.

00:02:44.755 --> 00:02:45.747
Who was the question?
- [India] Lucy.

00:02:45.747 --> 00:02:46.953
- Lucy that's your answer.

00:02:46.953 --> 00:02:47.802
I also--

00:02:47.802 --> 00:02:49.400
The majority of this entire team

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.926
is based on random shit.

00:02:50.926 --> 00:02:55.227
Like so, I think you just ask
as many times as possible.

00:02:55.227 --> 00:02:58.037
There are unlimited companies
in a world you can get

00:02:58.037 --> 00:03:00.080
to almost anybody because of Twitter,

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:01.635
again, a true social network.

00:03:01.635 --> 00:03:03.191
More so than comments on content

00:03:03.191 --> 00:03:05.304
which a lot of other platforms are.

00:03:05.304 --> 00:03:07.580
Email, at this point, I
think has been played out.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.739
It's harder to get to
people through email.

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:11.805
But that will still work too.

00:03:11.805 --> 00:03:13.268
I think it's stunning that you can get

00:03:13.268 --> 00:03:15.172
to most people in the world today.

00:03:15.172 --> 00:03:16.472
I don't think people,

00:03:16.472 --> 00:03:18.144
as many people are as wired as you and I.

00:03:18.144 --> 00:03:20.118
I think people have drawn the line to no

00:03:20.118 --> 00:03:21.906
but there's plenty.

00:03:21.906 --> 00:03:23.903
We're not the only two nice guys

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.946
believing in serendipity.

00:03:25.946 --> 00:03:28.546
There are tens of thousands
wildly accomplished

00:03:28.546 --> 00:03:31.843
CEOs, co-founders, that
will absolutely hire you

00:03:31.843 --> 00:03:36.000
on spec from one
request to get experience

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.602
whether they give you an internship

00:03:37.602 --> 00:03:39.529
or pay you minimum wage
or even give you a salary.

00:03:39.529 --> 00:03:41.085
It is a wide open field.

00:03:41.085 --> 00:03:42.455
It's about asking.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.574
- Yeah, I mean, I would
even complement what,

00:03:44.574 --> 00:03:46.784
everything Gary just said,
I'd complement that, Lucy

00:03:46.784 --> 00:03:49.583
by saying, you also have an
opportunity via these myriad

00:03:49.583 --> 00:03:51.719
social outlets and the
internet as a whole.

00:03:51.719 --> 00:03:54.343
Not just to reach out and contact people

00:03:54.343 --> 00:03:56.525
but to actually prove yourself.

00:03:56.525 --> 00:03:58.685
Like, if you need to show this experience

00:03:58.685 --> 00:04:00.310
that these people are seeking after,

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.424
just do it.

00:04:01.424 --> 00:04:03.096
You don't need someone's
permission to do that.

00:04:03.096 --> 00:04:06.300
If you wanna work in
construction, build something.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.319
If you wanna work in
an automotive factory,

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:10.735
work on cars.

00:04:10.735 --> 00:04:12.825
If you wanna be a filmmaker, make videos.

00:04:12.825 --> 00:04:15.588
You now have these multitude
of options in front of you

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.492
to show that you're capable.

00:04:17.492 --> 00:04:19.466
If you wanna be a writer, write something.

00:04:19.466 --> 00:04:20.812
- You know what happens
in that environment?

00:04:20.812 --> 00:04:22.089
If you actually have it,

00:04:22.089 --> 00:04:23.065
not everybody has it.

00:04:23.065 --> 00:04:24.388
But if you actually have it,

00:04:24.388 --> 00:04:25.735
you start getting into
a place very quickly

00:04:25.735 --> 00:04:27.105
that you realize, oh wait,

00:04:27.105 --> 00:04:29.287
I don't need to have a job
in the first place. (laughs)

00:04:29.287 --> 00:04:30.268
- That's right,

00:04:30.268 --> 00:04:33.513
no longer do you need the
runway to prove your worth on.

00:04:33.513 --> 00:04:35.208
You don't need someone else's approval,

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:36.694
you just do it yourself.

00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:39.341
Scary and very hard to do,

00:04:39.341 --> 00:04:42.243
it's not to be underestimated
just how challenging that is

00:04:42.243 --> 00:04:44.310
but it doesn't mean that
the opportunity isn't there

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:47.375
and that opportunity wasn't
there 10, 15 years ago.

00:04:47.375 --> 00:04:49.139
But it's uniquely there now.

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:50.834
- We're byproducts of that game.

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:53.156
- My entire career is
product of that game.

00:04:53.156 --> 00:04:54.944
- I had a liquor store
in New Jersey and got

00:04:54.944 --> 00:04:56.686
300 dollar camera at Best Buy

00:04:56.686 --> 00:04:58.543
and decided to make wine videos

00:04:58.543 --> 00:05:00.029
because I wanted to be like Emeril.

00:05:00.029 --> 00:05:01.554
- Wine videos.
- Wine videos.

00:05:01.554 --> 00:05:03.117
India, let's move it.

00:05:03.117 --> 00:05:04.905
Oh, by the way, I didn't get
weird there out of nowhere.

00:05:04.905 --> 00:05:07.320
We are streaming on
Facebook live right now.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.527
Be interesting to see--

00:05:08.527 --> 00:05:10.803
It's a whole different
dynamic 'cause these shows

00:05:10.803 --> 00:05:12.776
are consumed so much on Facebook live

00:05:12.776 --> 00:05:14.267
which launched yesterday.

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:15.795
India?

00:05:15.795 --> 00:05:17.091
- [Voiceover] Benjamin asks,

00:05:17.091 --> 00:05:18.833
"Where does confidence come from?

00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:20.644
"How do you both work on it?"

00:05:20.644 --> 00:05:22.408
- That's tough.

00:05:22.408 --> 00:05:23.546
- I'll let you go first here.

00:05:23.546 --> 00:05:24.475
(laughs)

00:05:24.475 --> 00:05:25.682
- Confidence, I mean--

00:05:25.682 --> 00:05:26.670
- Hold on.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.366
- [Voiceover] That's awesome.

00:05:28.366 --> 00:05:30.311
- Yeah, I couldn't (laughs)

00:05:31.362 --> 00:05:32.615
- You didn't know the address?

00:05:32.615 --> 00:05:35.239
- Gary, over your left shoulder
is my electric skateboard.

00:05:35.239 --> 00:05:36.353
Right there.
- Yes.

00:05:36.353 --> 00:05:38.323
- I rode that electric skateboard up here.

00:05:38.323 --> 00:05:40.347
And if there's one thing you
don't wanna do while traveling

00:05:40.347 --> 00:05:43.041
24 miles an hour in heavy
traffic through New York City,

00:05:43.041 --> 00:05:45.641
on an electric skateboard
is to whip out your phone

00:05:45.641 --> 00:05:46.849
and double check an address.

00:05:46.849 --> 00:05:47.754
- Respect.

00:05:47.754 --> 00:05:49.008
- So you gotta write that down.

00:05:49.008 --> 00:05:49.890
- Respect.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.817
All right, answer Ben's question
about your outrageous level

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:53.187
How does one have enough
confidence to ride

00:05:53.187 --> 00:05:56.484
an electronic skateboard 24
miles an hour in New York City?

00:05:56.484 --> 00:05:58.783
- I have an answer that's
not really a great one

00:05:58.783 --> 00:06:00.316
for people to hear, so I'm hoping you have

00:06:00.316 --> 00:06:01.360
a better answer than I do, Gary.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.730
My answer goes like this,

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.031
I'm one of four kids.

00:06:04.031 --> 00:06:05.424
There was the first born.

00:06:05.424 --> 00:06:06.492
The only daughter.

00:06:06.492 --> 00:06:07.444
And the baby.

00:06:07.444 --> 00:06:09.371
And then there's the
forgotten child, Casey.

00:06:09.371 --> 00:06:12.482
So in my household, it
was like fight to survive.

00:06:12.482 --> 00:06:14.827
And my confidence was like born into me

00:06:14.827 --> 00:06:18.241
out of need to just exist
and be noticed and be fed.

00:06:18.241 --> 00:06:21.515
Now, not everyone has had
the beautiful misfortune

00:06:21.515 --> 00:06:24.463
that yielded the fortune of my childhood

00:06:24.463 --> 00:06:26.576
that turned me into a confident person.

00:06:26.576 --> 00:06:28.712
But I think it's very
different from someone who

00:06:28.712 --> 00:06:32.219
finds themselves, as an
adult, in a world that sort of

00:06:32.219 --> 00:06:34.099
thrives on those who have confidence

00:06:34.099 --> 00:06:37.187
and being forced to find
that within yourself.

00:06:37.187 --> 00:06:40.067
But one shortcut I found to
that is making something.

00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:42.063
Making anything.

00:06:42.063 --> 00:06:43.271
Whether that's writing something,

00:06:43.271 --> 00:06:44.501
whether it's something creative,

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:46.011
whether it's something more pragmatic.

00:06:46.011 --> 00:06:47.172
Whether that's a relationship,

00:06:47.172 --> 00:06:48.449
whether that's a friendship.

00:06:48.449 --> 00:06:51.165
If you generate something
you can take sort of,

00:06:51.165 --> 00:06:53.371
you take comfort in what
it is that you've just made

00:06:53.371 --> 00:06:55.972
in your yield and I think
that's a really great shortcut

00:06:55.972 --> 00:06:57.086
to finding confidence.

00:06:57.086 --> 00:06:58.456
- Casey, answer--

00:06:58.456 --> 00:07:00.337
Give me a word association
play really quick here.

00:07:00.337 --> 00:07:02.543
Fear.

00:07:02.543 --> 00:07:04.563
- Illness.

00:07:04.563 --> 00:07:05.683
- Illness?

00:07:05.683 --> 00:07:06.568
- Yeah, that's--

00:07:06.568 --> 00:07:07.586
- I really didn't want you to go there.

00:07:07.586 --> 00:07:08.629
Thanks for screwing up my answer.

00:07:08.629 --> 00:07:09.465
(laughs)

00:07:09.465 --> 00:07:10.557
For me--

00:07:10.557 --> 00:07:12.661
- The only thing, being
sick is the only thing

00:07:12.661 --> 00:07:13.745
that I'm scared of.

00:07:13.745 --> 00:07:15.184
- By the way,
that's really funny.

00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:17.007
Actually, that's really interesting.

00:07:17.007 --> 00:07:18.897
Because I was dissing a little bit

00:07:18.897 --> 00:07:20.519
and now I'm gonna put you on a pedestal.

00:07:20.519 --> 00:07:22.839
It is literally the health and
well-being of the people I--

00:07:22.839 --> 00:07:25.486
Weirdly, for me, it's the people I love

00:07:25.486 --> 00:07:28.667
is scary ass crap for me.

00:07:28.667 --> 00:07:30.757
It's a very big challenge

00:07:30.757 --> 00:07:32.266
and we all go through it.

00:07:32.266 --> 00:07:34.008
And so, I'm with you on that.

00:07:34.008 --> 00:07:36.121
Where I was going with that, is this,

00:07:36.121 --> 00:07:39.342
I am not scared to fail,

00:07:39.342 --> 00:07:41.872
by any stretch of the imagination.

00:07:41.872 --> 00:07:45.094
And it comes in the form of
truly being in this weird place

00:07:45.094 --> 00:07:49.343
where I really don't give a
rat's ass what anybody thinks.

00:07:49.343 --> 00:07:51.201
And again, that's wiring.

00:07:51.201 --> 00:07:52.338
How does one work on that?

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:53.267
What do you think I sit--

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:55.357
What do you think I go in my room like,

00:07:55.357 --> 00:07:56.913
"Don't care what anybody thinks.

00:07:56.913 --> 00:07:58.608
Don't care what anybody--"

00:07:58.608 --> 00:07:59.629
(laughs)

00:07:59.629 --> 00:08:00.837
Like, you don't do that.

00:08:00.837 --> 00:08:02.485
- Yeah, you get made fun
of a lot in high school

00:08:02.485 --> 00:08:05.434
and it seems like the entire
world is falling apart

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:06.688
because you're being picked on.

00:08:06.688 --> 00:08:07.826
- I want people to make fun of me.

00:08:07.826 --> 00:08:09.822
- You grow up and it
realize it doesn't matter

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:11.192
what other people think.

00:08:11.192 --> 00:08:12.376
- I do, India.
- You really don't.

00:08:12.376 --> 00:08:13.470
It really doesn't.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.814
And appreciating that--

00:08:14.814 --> 00:08:16.393
- It's like those last
two weeks of high school.

00:08:16.393 --> 00:08:18.520
If you can capture that feeling.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.058
- Those last two weeks in high school,

00:08:20.058 --> 00:08:22.082
literally, everybody stops
caring what anybody thinks

00:08:22.082 --> 00:08:23.986
'cause you're all going somewhere else.

00:08:23.986 --> 00:08:26.401
And so, I've always had that feeling.

00:08:26.401 --> 00:08:28.746
It's crazy how, you know,

00:08:28.746 --> 00:08:31.137
I was born with confidence,
I truly believe that.

00:08:31.137 --> 00:08:34.876
I do believe, in my case, I
also have the fortunate aspects

00:08:34.876 --> 00:08:37.476
of coming from a struggle
place, in a different way.

00:08:37.476 --> 00:08:39.821
On the flip side, my mom,
I was the first born.

00:08:39.821 --> 00:08:41.586
The apple of my mom's eye.

00:08:41.586 --> 00:08:44.790
And so I had massive
positive reinforcement

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.575
which then just made me
feel entitled to success.

00:08:48.575 --> 00:08:50.525
In an environment where
I was failing classes.

00:08:50.525 --> 00:08:52.260
I was 4 foot 11 when I went

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.195
into my freshman year of high school.

00:08:53.195 --> 00:08:55.329
Not so strong...
- Rough, rough.

00:08:55.329 --> 00:08:56.615
-of a situation.
(laughs)

00:08:56.615 --> 00:08:57.676
But I walked out--

00:08:57.676 --> 00:08:59.740
I mean my book bag was bigger.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:01.277
Where's you big book bag?

00:09:01.277 --> 00:09:03.156
- Didn't bring it today,
not on the skateboard, Gary.

00:09:03.156 --> 00:09:04.457
- Like, I literally--

00:09:04.457 --> 00:09:06.082
My book bag was like your size.

00:09:06.082 --> 00:09:08.706
Let me tell you story
about my freshman year.

00:09:08.706 --> 00:09:10.772
Ninth day of school, I'm
walking down the hallway.

00:09:10.772 --> 00:09:12.119
I'm late for a class.

00:09:12.119 --> 00:09:13.907
I have a Jordache book bag

00:09:13.907 --> 00:09:14.780
